{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-3fbj1f","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3627y1+pm-3fbj1f+pm-ycgb5g","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-3fbj1f","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-wq9njf"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A mutation payload nested about 2,000 levels deep overflows the secret guard's recursive leaf walk, so block mode fails open and lets a nested credential through"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-17 while fixing pm-3fbj1f. scanMutationSecrets in src/sdk/mutation-guard.ts collects string leaves with a recursive walk (stringLeaves, recursion through Array.prototype.flatMap). A payload nested about 2,000 levels deep exceeds the call stack (measured on Node 26 with { token: { token: ... { note: \"<credential>\" } } }: RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded). evaluateMutationGuard catches every scanner exception and fails open by design (warning secret_guard_scan_failed_open, no findings), so in block mode a deeply nested credential is not blocked; only the advisory warning remains. JSON.parse accepts far deeper nesting, so an MCP or SDK payload can reach this depth. The failure is the traversal's own limit, not a detector failure the fail-open policy was written for. Fix direction: walk the payload with an explicit stack (keeping depth-first leaf order, so existing finding order is unchanged), apply the same to the key-named member pass added by pm-3fbj1f, and pin a depth well beyond the old limit in the guard spec. Whether a genuine detector failure should fail closed in block mode is a separate policy decision and out of scope. Duplicate check: searched secret guard fail open deep nesting stack overflow payload; pm-3fbj1f, pm-gh1699 and pm-jcz7qz are related and none owns traversal depth."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","mcp","robustness","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"scanMutationSecrets walks string leaves and key-named members with an explicit stack, so a payload nested far deeper than the call stack (at least 100,000 levels) is scanned without an exception; Findings keep their depth-first order and paths, so existing guard specs pass unchanged; In block mode a credential nested at that depth is blocked instead of producing secret_guard_scan_failed_open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A deeply nested credential is detected and blocked like a shallow one"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Nesting beyond about 2,000 levels throws RangeError inside the scan and the guard fails open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"secret-guard"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-3fbj1f","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1699","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jcz7qz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0f5771221c5fa0ef7e2b34728ed2ea2b83a8ae619ececb7b123558a4a4946919","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"bb1c565aee723654e25c10d10dcdcf8fa8adfea660dcd3b6b2b9b5b4c8e7897d"}
