{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T00:41:08.764Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3627y1+pm-3fbj1f+pm-wq9njf+pm-ycgb5g","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T00:41:08.764Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-17T00:41:08.759Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation (same branch as pm-3627y1, pm-ycgb5g and pm-3fbj1f, because the member pass added by pm-3fbj1f walks the same payload): stringLeaves now walks with an explicit stack. childSteps lists an array's elements (skipping holes, as the old flatMap did) or an object's own enumerable entries, and pushReversed pushes them in reverse one at a time, so the first child is walked first and a very wide object never spreads into one call. Leaves keep the old depth-first order, and an object is marked seen when it is walked, as before, so the existing guard specs pass unchanged. scanPayloadMembers uses the same walk with each step carrying its key context. The O(n^2) findIndex dedupe in scanMutationSecrets became a Set keyed by rule and path, with the same first-occurrence order. Measured on Node 26: a 100,000-level { token: ... } chain with a credential at the bottom scans in about 430 ms and evaluateMutationGuard in block mode throws mutation_secret_guard_blocked (before: RangeError near 2,000 levels, then secret_guard_scan_failed_open). A 100,000-key flat object takes about 2.46 s against 2.04 s for the released 2026.11.16 guard; the existing per-leaf token rules dominate, and the member pass adds about 20 percent. The spec pins a 100,000-level array chain (leaf rule) and object chain (member rule), block-mode refusal at that depth, and depth-first finding order across siblings and nesting.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"395c579c97ee1dea98c44a8f244dd7f1f21f4c9b570a528585e4efaae11ae846","after_hash":"0ce1878fcf411f72e147c8a70dbb71a458abacc32b925a9065b20ebf3babcd20","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"687beec37848260f4f674d3b31d976b2e60bec000a0ddbef9221e049b981c421"}
