{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T01:18:00.106Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3627y1+pm-3fbj1f+pm-wq9njf+pm-ycgb5g","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-17T01:18:00.106Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) found a fail-open regression in the first explicit-stack walk. childSteps called the payload array's own forEach, so an array whose forEach property was overridden (Object.assign([], { forEach: null })) threw inside the scan, and block mode returned secret_guard_scan_failed_open instead of blocking a token elsewhere in the payload. The merge base blocked it. childSteps now reads an array through Object.keys filtered to canonical index keys, which never calls a payload-owned method, skips holes, and costs only the present elements of a sparse array with length 2^32 - 1. The spec pins block-mode refusal with forEach, map, flatMap, filter, keys, entries and Symbol.iterator each overridden, a sparse array scanned in well under a second, and non-index array properties ignored as before.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T01:18:00.106Z"}],"before_hash":"5ddbcc02a0fe3102b6344b1c5c9f57e0935a39032b2145a947daac23419a3e81","after_hash":"46a45ded8c8aabce5f841230f49dd279a888c98dc56eaeebf7c59f24851973b1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f5943cb844d4abeca59f132bd9150aca39ddba5fc403d8848c00cdefa7a43139"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T01:49:13.493Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3627y1+pm-3fbj1f+pm-wq9njf+pm-ycgb5g","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-17T01:49:13.492Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1745 Greptile review (P1), fixed in b4374fe3b: reading arrays through Object.keys skipped non-enumerable elements, which the old flatMap walk and JSON.stringify both read. The digit-only filter also accepted 4294967295, which is not an array index. childSteps now uses Object.getOwnPropertyNames filtered to canonical indices no larger than 2^32 - 2. Payload-owned methods are still never called, and a sparse array still costs only its present elements. The spec pins a non-enumerable element and the out-of-range numeric key.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T01:49:13.493Z"}],"before_hash":"46a45ded8c8aabce5f841230f49dd279a888c98dc56eaeebf7c59f24851973b1","after_hash":"c7d8d532e5971176cd469c669d94d9efbc83f2101590b03b0544997af6bb1200","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_vers